### Jenosize Trend Writer — Jobs API, the whole fine-tuning workflow over HTTP.
###
### Run a request with "Send Request" in VS Code (REST Client extension) or
### the ▶ gutter icon in JetBrains IDEs. Set the two variables first:
###   @jobs  the URL printed by `make deploy-modal` (or http://localhost:8001 for `make jobs-dev`)
###   @key   your JOBS_API_KEY
### Jobs answer 202 with an "id": paste it into @run and poll "Run status".

@jobs = https://<workspace>--jenosize-trend-writer-jobs-api.modal.run
@key = <JOBS_API_KEY>
@run = <run id from a 202 response>
@vllm = https://<workspace>--jenosize-trend-writer-vllmserver.modal.run

### ─────────────────────────── 0. Setup (once) ───────────────────────────

### Liveness (no key needed)
GET {{jobs}}/health

### What the server resolved from its secrets (hosts and names, never values)
GET {{jobs}}/v1/config
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Every dependency, live: database + migrations, R2, labeller, adapters
GET {{jobs}}/v1/doctor
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Which migrations are applied
GET {{jobs}}/v1/migrations
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Apply pending migrations (idempotent)
POST {{jobs}}/v1/migrations/apply
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### ─────────────────────────── 1. Pull data ───────────────────────────

### Scrape: discover -> crawl -> clean. Only new/changed articles are written.
POST {{jobs}}/v1/scrape
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Re-check pages older than N days, to catch edits (0 = all of them)
POST {{jobs}}/v1/scrape
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"recheck_days": 30}

### Run status: result + per-stage stats (discover / crawl / clean)
GET {{jobs}}/v1/runs/{{run}}
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Recent runs (filter with ?kind=scrape|label|train|eval|publish)
GET {{jobs}}/v1/runs?limit=10
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Cancel a run
POST {{jobs}}/v1/runs/{{run}}/cancel
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### ─────────────────────────── 2. Inspect the corpus ───────────────────────────

### Progress per stage + last stage runs
GET {{jobs}}/v1/corpus
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Word counts, categories, and why articles were rejected
GET {{jobs}}/v1/corpus/stats
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Page through articles: state = all|pending|fetched|cleaned|rejected|duplicates|labelled
GET {{jobs}}/v1/corpus/articles?state=rejected&limit=20
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### One article in full: cleaned markdown, labels, signed link to the raw HTML
GET {{jobs}}/v1/corpus/article?url=https://www.jenosize.com/en/ideas/futurist/agentic-ai-guide-for-modern-business
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Random cleaned articles for review (same seed = same sample)
GET {{jobs}}/v1/corpus/sample?n=3
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### ─────────────────────────── 3. Labels ───────────────────────────

### Label ONE article without saving: check the prompt before paying for a run
POST {{jobs}}/v1/label/preview
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Label every new/changed article
POST {{jobs}}/v1/label
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Label audit: random labelled articles with their briefs
GET {{jobs}}/v1/corpus/sample?n=10&labelled=true
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### ─────────────────────────── 4. Dataset ───────────────────────────

### Publish v1 (201 published · 200 unchanged · 409 exists with other contents)
POST {{jobs}}/v1/datasets
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": "v1", "eval_frac": 0.1}

### Published versions
GET {{jobs}}/v1/datasets
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Re-validate v1 from R2
GET {{jobs}}/v1/datasets/v1/validate
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### The data card (markdown)
GET {{jobs}}/v1/datasets/v1/card
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Two rows exactly as the trainer sees them
GET {{jobs}}/v1/datasets/v1/examples?split=train&n=2
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### ─────────────────────────── 5. Train ───────────────────────────

### Cheap first run: 1 epoch, to prove the GPU path (~$0.50)
POST {{jobs}}/v1/train
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": "v1", "epochs": 1}

### Full run (writes /models/jeno-lora-v1)
POST {{jobs}}/v1/train
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": "v1", "epochs": 3, "lora_r": 16, "learning_rate": 0.0002}

### Trained adapters + their training metrics
GET {{jobs}}/v1/adapters
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### ─────────────────────────── 6. Serve & evaluate ───────────────────────────

### Point the `jeno-lora` alias at v1 (next vLLM cold start; jeno-lora-v1 works immediately)
POST {{jobs}}/v1/adapters/v1/activate
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### vLLM lists the base model + jeno-lora-v1 + jeno-lora (first call cold-starts 1-3 min)
GET {{vllm}}/v1/models
Authorization: Bearer <VLLM_API_KEY>

### Base vs jeno-lora-v1 on v1's held-out briefs
POST {{jobs}}/v1/eval
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": "v1", "endpoint": "{{vllm}}/v1"}

### Same, plus a blind judge (the labelling LLM grades base vs fine-tuned)
POST {{jobs}}/v1/eval
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": "v1", "endpoint": "{{vllm}}/v1", "judge": true}

### ─────────────────────────── 7. Publish ───────────────────────────

### Upload the evaluated adapter to Hugging Face
POST {{jobs}}/v1/adapters/v1/publish
X-API-Key: {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": "v1", "repo_id": "<your-hf-user>/jeno-trend-writer-lora"}
